WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.710
One, two, three, four!

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.880
Five, six, seven, eight!

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.490
One, two, three, four!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.490
How did it end up like this?

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.490
Isn't it refreshing?

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:26.400
I never imagined you'd suggest something like this.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.560
Wait, that was rude of me.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.410
It just came to mind. I didn't mean to make a big deal out of it.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.560
No, no, we should take advantage of good ideas right away.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.510
Like this!

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.580
Today feels like it'll be a good day.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.800
Thank you, Miss Yoshinoya.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.270
It was nothing.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.280
No, I think it was a wonderful idea.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.530
Really?

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.540
Yes, so let's keep doing it.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.300
Okay.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.040
Same time tomorrow morning, okay?

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.170
Okay!

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.970
We're all waiting.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.380
Send.

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.550
Yunocchi, can I come in?

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.730
Sure, Miya.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.740
I just can't keep still.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:32.980
Hey, what time is she getting here?

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.860
Chika? Look!

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.910
Is that from Kabuki-za?

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.500
She sure is active.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.250
She went alone today?

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:49.040
Yeah. She's got to be completely absorbed in the show right now.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.300
It's been a while since Chika's come over.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.060
Yeah, she can't make it over that often.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.690
Chika's a first year in high school like us, right?

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:12.390
Yeah. Last time she came was during spring
break when she was still in middle school.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.110
What's she like?

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.280
She's really cute.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.890
Does she look like Sae?

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.030
Yeah, a bit.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.620
But she's more Hiro's height.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.130
What?

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:26.060
We're just talking about Sae and Chika.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.120
Hold on.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.630
All right, it's done.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:31.960
What was it?

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.960
Sae and Chika really resemble each other, don't they?

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.090
Yeah, especially their personalities.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.040
You can tell they're sisters just by looking at them.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.410
That's right.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:48.940
They're both frank and stubborn.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.980
But maybe Chika's changed since she got to high school.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.860
Nazuna, what's wrong?

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.860
I'm just a bit nervous.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.540
I'm back.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.080
Hello!

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:06.870
They're here!

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.380
Yuno, Miyako, Hiro! Good to see you again!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.380
Chika! You're all dressed up today.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.760
Oh, not really.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.140
I just went to Kabuki-za today.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.390
Welcome!

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.920
Come on in. I just finished the paella.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.520
Thanks for having me over again!

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.720
I can't believe it! It's like a party!

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.030
It's always such a mess having you over.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.340
That's not true.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.710
Here, Chika.

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:43.780
Thanks.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.040
Let's eat!

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:50.360
I was so busy earlier that I didn't have a chance to introduce you.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.000
Why don't we do that now?

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.290
You first, Nori.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.800
Pleased to meet you. I'm Nori.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.550
I'm a first year in the art program.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.020
Pleased to meet you. I'm Chika.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.050
I'm sure we'll get along fine.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.050
This is Nazuna.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.970
Uh... I'm Nazuna.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.420
Pleased to meet you.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.060
I'm a first year in Gen Ed.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.060
Gen Ed? That's the same as me.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.820
Nice to meet you! I'm Miyako, a second year in the art program.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.130
My talents are eating and eating.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.570
Oh, I know that!

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.300
Sorry to always impose on you like this.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:33.080
Don't worry. You rarely make it out here, so we should have something good.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.250
So, how was the kabuki?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.590
Well, it was like...

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.840
"If you didn't know, you should ask."

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:47.570
Kiku's line! I can still hear it ringing in my ears!

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.720
I thought I was gonna start crying.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.640
You got good seats, huh?

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.850
Yeah, right by the aisle.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:57.940
Wow, you know a lot about kabuki.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.890
No, this is the first time I've gone to Kabuki-za.

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:04.200
I just used to watch it on TV.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:09.010
We went on a field trip in middle school.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:12.250
But I think that was to the National Theatre.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.960
I don't really remember.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:18.980
Kabuki, huh? We used to watch that on TV on New Year's Day.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.460
I'm surprised you went alone, Chika.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.470
Well, I am in high school now.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:28.350
Weren't you nervous going alone?

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:32.390
No, not really. I was fine.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.080
That's amazing.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.570
If I didn't have family or friends with me, I wouldn't be able to calm down.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.570
Sometimes, I feel like that too.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.610
I'm so full! That was great.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.240
Thanks!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.000
Shall I make tea?

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.750
Would you like coffee, black tea, or green tea?

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.750
I'm fine with black tea.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.000
Me too!

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.010
Was what you watched like this?

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.010
Not at all!

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:13.520
Friar Benten is a famous bandit like Ishikawa Goemon or the Rat Boy.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:18.530
He's supposed to be a really hot guy in a flower print kimono.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.200
Really?

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.960
He was so dreamy!

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.030
I wish I could draw him.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.530
Yeah, that'd be great.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.530
You think so too?

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:35.860
Yeah, I'm jealous of all these artists.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.420
Well, everyone has their own talents.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.920
Gen Ed is fun too, right?

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.210
Yeah!

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:46.220
Does Yamabuki High do school events as a group?

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:50.970
I think so. They always say that Gen Ed is better at field day.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.600
You'll be our enemy in the fall, Nazuna!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.120
She won't be our enemy.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:04.610
But didn't you say that we don't stand a chance against Gen Ed?

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.100
Don't stand a chance?

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.360
Don't worry, Nazuna.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.370
Sae was just a sore loser.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.370
A sore loser?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:20.460
I see, sis. The art department just sucks.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.130
That's not true!

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.750
Maybe I should start cheering for Gen Ed.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:26.360
Um, um... It's still only May.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.380
Fine, you can stay at home and do that.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:30.400
I can't believe you, sis!

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.390
You keep getting in people's faces.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.390
You're the one who can't take a joke!

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.850
I haven't seen sibling rivalry in a while!

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:40.390
Feels nostalgic.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.880
I think I know what Hiro meant.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:48.740
Yeah, they really are alike.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.240
Would everyone like some cake?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.240
I do!

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.750
Chiffon cake!

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.540
The bakery nearby just started making it.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.880
Yuno, want to cut it?

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.380
Sure!

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.630
Um, how do I cut it into sevenths?

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.000
Should I calculate it?

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.180
Just do it by eye.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:19.190
Just cut it into eighths and give me the extra piece!

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:20.520
Oh, Miya!

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.270
It should be about fifty-one degrees, right?

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.930
How did you figure that out?

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:34.780
This is the first time I've eaten fifty-one degree cake.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.120
Me too.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.040
It's always nice to try new things.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.790
Hey...

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.210
You were in brass band in middle school, right?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.040
What instrument did you play?

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.050
Alto sax.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:51.050
It took so long before I was able to get a good tone out of it.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:53.800
Practicing must've been tough.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:59.560
It was so hard that I wanted to quit.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.930
But somehow, you're still going.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:04.940
Yeah, it's fun playing with everyone.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:08.190
Right now, we're practicing Holst's Jupiter.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:11.940
Sorry, I'm nerding out, aren't I?

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.470
No, you're fine.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:18.950
Well, I wanted to say so, but maybe I'm a little too late.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.450
I also do that.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:25.780
Oh, really? Sorry, I'm just going on about myself.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.580
Don't worry.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.590
You've always been full of yourself, haven't you?

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:32.840
I think the word you're looking for is "ambitious."

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:38.600
You've always fit in really well here, haven't you, Chika?

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.800
I've heard so much about you.

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:46.440
And besides, my sister is here.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:49.480
But you pick a fight with me the second you show up.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.370
And then you come stay in my room.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.610
That's right! Couch surfing for a night!

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.740
You're such a pain.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.870
You always say that.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:06.040
Anyway, I'm happy I fit in with you.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.620
Well, we are the same age.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:08.630
Yeah.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:15.340
Chika, do you have any plans for tomorrow?

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:17.810
No, I haven't decided yet.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.510
Is there anywhere you'd like to go?

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:26.890
How about we all go out? Bring lunches and make it a picnic?

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.190
A picnic?

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.810
Lunches!

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:34.840
How does that sound to you, Nazuna?

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:35.530
Fine!

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:38.530
I wonder what the weather's supposed to be like.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.280
Hold on a sec...

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.660
It's supposed to be sunny.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:48.420
Nazuna, do you know a park or something around here that would be good for a picnic?

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:52.040
Um... How about Kawasemi Park?

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:56.630
We'd have to take the bus, but there's a lake where we can ride boats.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.040
Wow, you really are a townie.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.920
A townie? You mean a local?

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.650
That's what we called them back home too.

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:08.140
I guess the word for it is different everywhere.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:10.860
Anyway, shall I make sandwiches for tomorrow?

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.690
I just bought bread.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.440
Sure! Er, I'll help out too.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:17.070
Me too.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:18.450
Me too!

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:22.200
All right, why don't we all get together in my room tomorrow morning?

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.450
Sure!

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:25.790
That was great.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:26.950
See you tomorrow.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:27.990
Good night.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.210
Good night!

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:32.920
See you tomorrow!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:34.290
Yeah!

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.930
One, two, three, four!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:46.720
Five, six, seven, eight!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:46.720
Uh, Principal?

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:47.680
What is it?

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:49.800
Do we have to do this tomorrow too?

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:57.070
Of course. If you're going to be out here working hard, I should too.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.320
I can't take this anymore.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:05.710
You've made such an impression on me.

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:07.330
If I don't live up to your example...

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.330
Shall we run fifty dashes?

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.480
We're back!

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:37.570
That was fun.

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:39.360
The weather was great too.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.820
Chika, are you staying until evening?

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.990
Would you like to have tea or something?

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.240
All right then, I want to see Nori and Nazuna's rooms!

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.700
How about mine first?

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.870
It's a bit of a mess, but...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:57.500
Now I'm a bit worried. I'll go clean up first.

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:00.010
Why don't you come up in about ten minutes?

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:05.260
I don't have enough cups for everyone, so can you bring your own?

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.840
I'm glad it wasn't too messy.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.180
Norippe!

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:18.400
It's open.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.230
Sorry to bother you.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:21.400
Come on in.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.990
There's no handle, but it's still a cup!

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.990
Miya, that's not quite right.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.910
You have your own computer? That must be nice.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.270
Your family has one?

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:40.230
Yeah. I want my own, but I can't afford it on my New Year's money.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.670
It was the same for me.

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:43.920
Here, how about some nice springy snacks?

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.180
Oh, kashiwa mochi!

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:51.510
This is the kind of thing you can only have at this time of year.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:55.350
Really? The supermarket has them all year round.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.230
Sakura mochi too.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:01.980
Oh yeah, there were lots of carp banners
on the way to the park, weren't there?

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:03.990
Tomorrow is Children's Day, after all.

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.980
Non, non! Isn't Children's Day today?

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:08.240
Huh? Why?

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.240
After all, we're playing around like we're kids again!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.000
Miya, I think you're going a bit too far back.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.250
I was afraid you'd run into something and hurt yourself on the boat.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:20.500
Sorry, Yunocchi. It just felt so good.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:24.010
You sure are energetic, Miyako.

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:28.510
You were paddling all over. How far did you go?

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:32.010
I went all the way to the end, touched it, and then came back.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.890
All the way to the end?

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:37.750
Was there a big turtle there?

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:38.940
I didn't see one.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.690
A big turtle?

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:45.280
Sometimes a big turtle that's like the master of the lake comes out.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:49.200
They say that if you touch its shell, you'll get rich.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:54.160
Oh man, if I'd known, I'd have caught him!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.950
You can't catch the turtle!

00:14:55.950 --> 00:15:00.130
So we were on the other end from Yuno and Miyako?

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:02.550
Yeah. There were a lot of ducks.

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:04.340
Yeah, tons of them.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:07.090
So, what did you three talk about?

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.550
It's a secret!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:14.470
Um, well, school and stuff like that.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:17.320
That's right. By the way, Chika...

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.020
Can we tell them about that?

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.400
Huh? That what?

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:23.900
If everyone at Hidamari Apartments were an animal...

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.400
Oh, that!

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:27.530
But...

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.650
It'll be fine. It was funny.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:30.660
What?

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:31.800
Animals?

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.160
Now I'm curious.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:36.410
Well, Hiro's a swallow.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:37.790
A swallow?

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:41.540
They're always so busy feeding their chicks.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:42.790
How about me?

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:46.050
Miyako is totally free, so she's a cat.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.260
Yuno is a hamster.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:50.760
A hamster?

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:54.840
The image of a tiny, cute, hard worker.

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.010
We all agreed.

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:58.020
A hard worker...

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.020
So, what am I?

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:04.900
You're always up late and stuck to your desk, so you're a gecko!

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:08.650
I knew this was a bad idea.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:12.410
Well, they say that geckos keep the house safe.

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:18.410
Yeah, that's it! I'm sure you keep Hidamari Apartments safe, right?

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:21.660
Right, right. That's it.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.170
Now you're just making things up.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:27.540
But swallows are smart. That's a good one.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.200
Do I have to be a hamster?

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.050
Beats being a gecko.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:36.170
Anyway, Chika, did you say anything else you shouldn't have?

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:43.270
No. After that, we talked about dumplings, brass band, and computers, right?

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:44.480
Yeah.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.480
Liar.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:51.440
They really are all the same age, getting along so easily.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:52.700
That's nice.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:53.770
Yeah!

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:58.930
Hiro, Sae, what did you talk about?

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:00.820
Huh? Us?

00:17:00.820 --> 00:17:02.980
What did we talk about?

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:08.630
We just stopped the boat under a tree and relaxed.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:12.380
Yeah. Things like, "The water's still pretty chilly, isn't it?"

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:17.640
Nazuna and I talked about how striking you two are.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:18.890
Striking?

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:23.390
Yeah. Sae is so cool, and Hiro is so elegant.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.560
It's like you're straight out of a movie.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:29.150
What are you guys talking about?

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:31.400
Wow, you're blushing!

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:32.980
Chika!

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.740
That makes me happy.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:38.670
And to think, we didn't talk about anything important at all.

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:41.830
Didn't we talk about anything else?

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:45.970
Just about how Kawasemi Park really is full of kingfishers.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:48.510
And how much fun it looked like Chika and the others were having.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.550
And then, how wonderful the breeze felt.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.300
And what we'd do tomorrow.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.260
How wonderful!

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:59.050
Just like in one of Sae's stories!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:05.350
Like when the lead couple went to Oze and talked while taking a stroll.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:10.110
They didn't talk about anything special, but it was so touching.

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.470
You read that?

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:14.400
Yeah, I borrowed Yuno's copy.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:15.990
Thanks.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.990
All right, I'm heading home.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:25.790
Thanks for having me over, everyone!

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.210
See you later!

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:28.530
It was fun!

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:29.790
Visit again sometime!

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:32.780
You're sure I shouldn't come with you?

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:34.300
Yeah, the station is close.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.260
Let's talk sometime.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.050
Sure.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.010
I'll text you.

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.050
Okay! I will too.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.570
Take care, okay?

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:44.350
Will you be back for summer vacation?

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:48.010
Sure! Next time, I'll stay longer.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.610
Thanks again!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.440
Are those your teachers?

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:57.950
Why are they together?

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.370
Hello, everyone.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:01.950
Hello.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.820
Are you trying to train Miss Yoshinoya?

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:10.250
No, no. This was all her idea.

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:15.460
How did it end up like this?

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:20.970
You should all learn from Miss Yoshinoya.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:25.380
I can't let her get ahead of me, either!

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:27.280
Anyway, I'll be taking my leave now.

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:30.480
I'm not doing this again tomorrow!

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.720
Today went by so fast.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.370
It was busy with so many people around.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:51.740
Chika seemed a little different.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.380
I guess she grew up a bit.

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:05.010
I'm glad Chika, Nori, and Nazuna got along so well.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:10.890
I wonder if I seemed like an upperclassman.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:16.650
And thus, we traversed the unexplored Lake Kawasemi!

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.920
I'm glad we didn't fall in.

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:19.900
It was so calm.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.650
I don't want to go home now.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.070
What if you don't?

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.670
I'll make dinner.

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:25.420
Yay!

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:27.300
Wow, there's so many.

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:29.350
Yeah, thanks to Nazuna.

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:30.330
Eh? But...

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.250
I'm glad we all went together.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.920
Yeah, it was so much fun with all of us together.

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:50.270
And send.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.260
I wonder if I'll be sore tomorrow.

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:05.950
That was fun.

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:15.060
Victor Hugo said, "The fortune of well-being is like eating nothing but bread."

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:16.280
What's that suppossed to mean?

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:17.420
You mean, no snacks?

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.730
I have bread for a snack and then rice for dinner!

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:23.070
I get it! You need a balanced diet, right?

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:26.660
That's it. Having many pleasures is the spice of life.

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:28.430
That's deep.

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:32.080
Next time, "May 13th~14th: Yuno Crab" and

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:35.810
"September 26th~27th: Eggplants Really Are Great."

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:39.970
We'll be waiting at Yamabuki High. Be sure to come see us!
